  {
   "id": "https://nealcaren.github.io/paperpress-demo/iiif/suffragist/1917-01-24/canvas/p11/text/r1",
   "type": "Annotation",
   "motivation": "supplementing",
   "body": {
    "type": "TextualBody",
    "value": "Johnstone—New York Evening World, January 17",
    "format": "text/plain"
   },
   "target": "https://nealcaren.github.io/paperpress-demo/iiif/suffragist/1917-01-24/canvas/p11#xywh=1203,2693,2386,128"
  },
  {
   "id": "https://nealcaren.github.io/paperpress-demo/iiif/suffragist/1917-01-24/canvas/p11/text/r2",
   "type": "Annotation",
   "motivation": "supplementing",
   "body": {
    "type": "TextualBody",
    "value": "An Ungraceful Position",
    "format": "text/plain"
   },
   "target": "https://nealcaren.github.io/paperpress-demo/iiif/suffragist/1917-01-24/canvas/p11#xywh=3501,3016,1406,165"
  },
  {
   "id": "https://nealcaren.github.io/paperpress-demo/iiif/suffragist/1917-01-24/canvas/p11/text/r3",
   "type": "Annotation",
   "motivation": "supplementing",
   "body": {
    "type": "TextualBody",
    "value": "R. WILSON, more than any other Presi- M dent, has taken the initiative in legislation. Less than half a year ago he surprised his party out of its boots by proclaiming the eight-hour day principle. Now-he repeats his pious regrets and tactless excuses over being unable to lend more than a private voice to the suffrage cause.",
    "format": "text/plain"
   },
   "target": "https://nealcaren.github.io/paperpress-demo/iiif/suffragist/1917-01-24/canvas/p11#xywh=3101,3307,2232,1274"
  },
  {
   "id": "https://nealcaren.github.io/paperpress-demo/iiif/suffragist/1917-01-24/canvas/p11/text/r4",
   "type": "Annotation",
   "motivation": "supplementing",
   "body": {
    "type": "TextualBody",
    "value": "The suffragists have a right to feel peevish. Without hoping that their campaign makes Mr. Wilson nervous, one may hope it makes him conscious of his ungraceful position on an important domestic issue.—Boston Journal, January 10.",
    "format": "text/plain"
   },
   "target": "https://nealcaren.github.io/paperpress-demo/iiif/suffragist/1917-01-24/canvas/p11#xywh=3101,4621,2414,1046"
  },
  {
   "id": "https://nealcaren.github.io/paperpress-demo/iiif/suffragist/1917-01-24/canvas/p11/text/r5",
   "type": "Annotation",
   "motivation": "supplementing",
   "body": {
    "type": "TextualBody",
    "value": "HE silent sentinels have progressed. They have reached the point where there are violent protests against them. Everybody knows that a movement is really on its feet when the world divides itself into factions and begins wrangling over it. Recall in this connection the movement for the higher education of women, the emancipation of women, and so on.— Moary Brush Williams, in New York Tribune, December 14.",
    "format": "text/plain"
   },
   "target": "https://nealcaren.github.io/paperpress-demo/iiif/suffragist/1917-01-24/canvas/p11#xywh=3107,5939,2226,1600"
  },
  {
   "id": "https://nealcaren.github.io/paperpress-demo/iiif/suffragist/1917-01-24/canvas/p11/text/r6",
   "type": "Annotation",
   "motivation": "supplementing",
   "body": {
    "type": "TextualBody",
    "value": "Wilson and the Pickets",
    "format": "text/plain"
   },
   "target": "https://nealcaren.github.io/paperpress-demo/iiif/suffragist/1917-01-24/canvas/p11#xywh=3101,7539,2414,429"
  },
  {
   "id": "https://nealcaren.github.io/paperpress-demo/iiif/suffragist/1917-01-24/canvas/p11/text/r7",
   "type": "Annotation",
   "motivation": "supplementing",
   "body": {
    "type": "TextualBody",
    "value": "R. WILSON only smiles at the suffrage M pickets—who, doubtless, remember that she who laughs last laughs best—Boston Journal, January 10.",
    "format": "text/plain"
   },
   "target": "https://nealcaren.github.io/paperpress-demo/iiif/suffragist/1917-01-24/canvas/p11#xywh=3101,8059,2414,821"
  },
  {
   "id": "https://nealcaren.github.io/paperpress-demo/iiif/suffragist/1917-01-24/canvas/p11/text/r8",
   "type": "Annotation",
   "motivation": "supplementing",
   "body": {
    "type": "TextualBody",
    "value": "F Mr. Wilson had picketed Mexico as well as I the suffragists picket the White House, all would be well.—Boston Journal, January 18.",
    "format": "text/plain"
   },
   "target": "https://nealcaren.github.io/paperpress-demo/iiif/suffragist/1917-01-24/canvas/p11#xywh=3123,9155,2213,405"
  },
  {
   "id": "https://nealcaren.github.io/paperpress-demo/iiif/suffragist/1917-01-24/canvas/p11/text/r11",
   "type": "Annotation",
   "motivation": "supplementing",
   "body": {
    "type": "TextualBody",
    "value": "Philadelphia Evening Bulletin, January 16",
    "format": "text/plain"
   },
   "target": "https://nealcaren.github.io/paperpress-demo/iiif/suffragist/1917-01-24/canvas/p11#xywh=1800,10560,1904,123"
  },
  {
   "id": "https://nealcaren.github.io/paperpress-demo/iiif/suffragist/1917-01-24/canvas/p11/text/r12",
   "type": "Annotation",
   "motivation": "supplementing",
   "body": {
    "type": "TextualBody",
    "value": "Demands Now: Not Requests EA men! Yea menl Yea menl Fight 'em, Y Fight 'em, Fight 'em.\" This is a yell used by the student body at Ann Arbor during a football game. It is inspiring rather than pugnacious. It nerves the football squad into a fighting, though not pugilistic spirit.",
    "format": "text/plain"
   },
   "target": "https://nealcaren.github.io/paperpress-demo/iiif/suffragist/1917-01-24/canvas/p11#xywh=776,3016,2227,1181"
  },
  {
   "id": "https://nealcaren.github.io/paperpress-demo/iiif/suffragist/1917-01-24/canvas/p11/text/r13",
   "type": "Annotation",
   "motivation": "supplementing",
   "body": {
    "type": "TextualBody",
    "value": "This same yell, with a minor change, seems to have been adopted by the equal suffrage women of the United States as represented by the Woman's Party. If they do not yell it, they think it deep down in their hearts, this way: “Yea women! Yea women! Yea women! Fight 'em, Fight 'em, Fight 'em.\"",
    "format": "text/plain"
   },
   "target": "https://nealcaren.github.io/paperpress-demo/iiif/suffragist/1917-01-24/canvas/p11#xywh=779,4213,2229,958"
  },
  {
   "id": "https://nealcaren.github.io/paperpress-demo/iiif/suffragist/1917-01-24/canvas/p11/text/r14",
   "type": "Annotation",
   "motivation": "supplementing",
   "body": {
    "type": "TextualBody",
    "value": "That is the spirit of the women of today toward the dominant political party. They are no longer attempting to catch the support of the national congress by soft soap and taffy methods. In order to be properly heard, they must make themselves feared at the polls.",
    "format": "text/plain"
   },
   "target": "https://nealcaren.github.io/paperpress-demo/iiif/suffragist/1917-01-24/canvas/p11#xywh=781,5184,2224,816"
  },
  {
   "id": "https://nealcaren.github.io/paperpress-demo/iiif/suffragist/1917-01-24/canvas/p11/text/r15",
   "type": "Annotation",
   "motivation": "supplementing",
   "body": {
    "type": "TextualBody",
    "value": "There is nothing which makes a politician sit up and take notice more than threatened defeat at the polls. The only way in which some men in office can be reached, is by a threat to retire him to private office. Men in office worship at the shrine of Strength and laugh at Weakness.",
    "format": "text/plain"
   },
   "target": "https://nealcaren.github.io/paperpress-demo/iiif/suffragist/1917-01-24/canvas/p11#xywh=781,6019,2219,954"
  },
  {
   "id": "https://nealcaren.github.io/paperpress-demo/iiif/suffragist/1917-01-24/canvas/p11/text/r16",
   "type": "Annotation",
   "motivation": "supplementing",
   "body": {
    "type": "TextualBody",
    "value": "The women of America, demanding the vote, realize that much of their efforts have been wasted in the past by their docility and lambweakness. Now they are more militaristic. They do not hesitate to call a spade a spade and to denounce those who they think should be denounced. They do not stop even at the President of the United States, if they think he deserves criticism.",
    "format": "text/plain"
   },
   "target": "https://nealcaren.github.io/paperpress-demo/iiif/suffragist/1917-01-24/canvas/p11#xywh=776,6992,2224,1224"
  },
  {
   "id": "https://nealcaren.github.io/paperpress-demo/iiif/suffragist/1917-01-24/canvas/p11/text/r17",
   "type": "Annotation",
   "motivation": "supplementing",
   "body": {
    "type": "TextualBody",
    "value": "Women must demand, nowadays. Requests are too often lost on the four winds—Bay City, Michigan, Tribune, December 8.",
    "format": "text/plain"
   },
   "target": "https://nealcaren.github.io/paperpress-demo/iiif/suffragist/1917-01-24/canvas/p11#xywh=781,8243,2219,354"
  },
  {
   "id": "https://nealcaren.github.io/paperpress-demo/iiif/suffragist/1917-01-24/canvas/p11/text/r18",
   "type": "Annotation",
   "motivation": "supplementing",
   "body": {
    "type": "TextualBody",
    "value": "Watchful Waiting",
    "format": "text/plain"
   },
   "target": "https://nealcaren.github.io/paperpress-demo/iiif/suffragist/1917-01-24/canvas/p11#xywh=1381,8752,1067,163"
  },
  {
   "id": "https://nealcaren.github.io/paperpress-demo/iiif/suffragist/1917-01-24/canvas/p11/text/r19",
   "type": "Annotation",
   "motivation": "supplementing",
   "body": {
    "type": "TextualBody",
    "value": "HE vigil of the women suffragists outside the White House grounds must come under the head of watchful waiting.—Philadelphia Press, January 18.",
    "format": "text/plain"
   },
   "target": "https://nealcaren.github.io/paperpress-demo/iiif/suffragist/1917-01-24/canvas/p11#xywh=787,9027,2221,544"
  },
  {
